// Loose ground really flies: a charge set on a tunnel floor next to a bed of sand. The push runs into the
// bed (fading over half a metre) and throws it out and up, away from the charge: dozens of tiles of sand
// are in the air at once, the bed near the charge is scoured to the rock, and it all comes down again
// further along (none is lost: the floor is bedrock, so none falls through a cracked floor).
map
############################################################
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#.@........................................................#
#..................sssssssssssssssssssssss.................#
#..................sssssssssssssssssssssss.................#
BBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBB
end
expect 1 count:Sand == 46
explode 5 16 0 0.5                // on the floor, a metre short of the bed
expect 6 debris:Sand >= 15        // in flight: a third of the bed or more
expect 6 is:17,0,Sand == 0        // the near end is blown off down to the rock
expect 6 is:17,1,Sand == 0
expect 6 is:20,1,Sand == 0
expect 120 debris == 0            // all of it has landed
expect 120 count:Sand == 46       // none lost
expect 120 is:18,1,Sand == 0      // and it lies further off: the near end is still bare
